assumptions, caller-supplied init code, and deployment rejection checks, making 
authorization bypass, deterministic-address collisions, or malicious 
implementation deployment important to assess before revisiting already 
completed components. EXIT CRITERIA: Trace constructor trust initialization and 
every public deployment path, verify authorization cannot be bypassed, confirm 
CREATE2 salts and init code cannot cause unsafe collisions or substitute 
unintended bytecode, and establish that successful deployments always produce 
the intended contract type with no exploitable post-deployment trust or 
ownership configuration.

